---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
import { isTodo } from '../lib/format';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy/' },
];
const updated = 'September 2026';
const brokerageMissing = isTodo(site.brokerage.legalName);
---

<Page
  title="Privacy Notice"
  description="How Kirby Chan and Co. collects, uses and protects personal information under PIPEDA and how consent works for electronic messages under CASL."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  h1="Privacy notice"
  accent="Privacy"
  lede={`How we collect, use and protect personal information and how you can withdraw consent at any time. Last updated ${updated}.`}
  crumbs={crumbs}
  tone="sand"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap-narrow prose">
      <div class="notice">
        <p>
          <strong>Have a lawyer review this before launch.</strong> This notice is written to align
          with the Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act and Canada's
          Anti-Spam Legislation and it describes how this website works. It is not legal advice
          and it has not been reviewed by counsel.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name}{brokerageMissing ? ' [TODO: brokerage legal name]' : `, ${site.brokerage.legalName}`}.
        Registered office: {site.office.street}, {site.office.city}, {site.office.region}{' '}
        {site.office.postalCode}. Phone {site.contact.phone}. Email {site.contact.email}.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are responsible for the personal information under our control. If you have a question
        about this notice or about how we handle your information, contact us using the details
        above.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Information you give us.</strong> Your name, email address, phone number, the
          neighbourhood and timeline you select and anything you write in the message field of an
          enquiry form.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Information about your enquiry.</strong> The page you submitted from, the date and
          time, the country your request came from and your browser user agent string. We use this
          to reply in context and to identify automated submissions.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Spam prevention.</strong> Our enquiry form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to
          distinguish people from automated scripts. Cloudflare processes a challenge token for
          this purpose.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This site does not use advertising cookies, analytics cookies or third party tracking
        scripts. No cookie consent banner appears because no non-essential cookies are set.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
      <p>
        To answer your enquiry, to provide real estate services you have asked us about and, where
        you have consented, to send you information about Markham real estate. We do not use your
        information for any other purpose without asking you first.
      </p>

      <h2>Consent and how to withdraw it</h2>
      <p>
        We ask for express consent on our enquiry form before we contact you with commercial
        electronic messages. That consent is recorded with your submission.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can withdraw consent at any time. Use the unsubscribe link in any email we send, reply
        to any message asking us to stop or write to {site.contact.email}. We will action it
        promptly. Withdrawing consent to marketing messages does not prevent us from replying to a
        transaction you have engaged us on.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        Your enquiry is forwarded to our customer relationship system so we can track and answer
        it. We use service providers to host this website, to filter spam and to manage client
        records and those providers process information on our behalf under contract.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal information. We do not share it with third parties for their own
        marketing.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you engage us for a transaction, information may be shared with the parties needed to
        complete it, such as lawyers, lenders, the brokerage and the real estate board and may be
        subject to the rules of the Toronto Regional Real Estate Board and applicable legislation.
      </p>

      <h2>Where information is stored</h2>
      <p>
        Our service providers may store or process information outside Canada, including in the
        United States. Where that happens, the information may be accessible to courts and law
        enforcement in that jurisdiction under its laws.
      </p>
      <p>
        This website is hosted by Cloudflare, which also processes the enquiry form and provides
        spam protection. Enquiries sent through the form are passed to the system our team uses to
        manage client enquiries. Our main website, kirbychanandco.com, is operated on the Lofty
        platform and has its own privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep enquiry records for as long as needed to answer you and to meet our record keeping
        obligations as a registrant, then we delete or de-identify them. Records connected to a
        completed transaction are retained for the period required by law.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask us what personal information we hold about you, ask us to correct it or ask us
        to delete it where we are not required to keep it. Write to {site.contact.email} and we
        will respond within a reasonable time, normally within thirty days.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are not satisfied with our response, you may contact the Office of the Privacy
        Commissioner of Canada.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        This site is served over HTTPS. Enquiries are validated and filtered server side and
        secrets such as webhook addresses and spam filtering keys are held in server configuration
        and are never exposed in the pages you load.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
      <p>
        If we change how we handle personal information we will update this page and change the
        date at the top.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
